From: Brian.Hawthorne@east.sun.com (Brian Holt Hawthorne - SunSelect Engineering)
Subject: talk.extropians... NOT!

If we wish to have a sci.extropians, soc.extropians, talk.extropians,
or whatever, we can do so without any call for votes at all.

You see, there is this little loophole called INET distribution
newsgroups. Years ago, when Erik Fair created NNTP, many of the
Internet backbone sites were worried about massive amounts of 
Usenet traffic (the net was much slower then). Erik argued that
people were going to transmit this traffic anyway, and if they
couldn't do it with NNTP, they would create gateways and mailing
lists and there would be many more copies bouncing around. He
was very convincing. At the same time, he suggested that it
be possible to take existing Internet mailing lists and fast-track
them into Usenet newsgroups with a distribution of 'inet'. Since
these groups would only go across NNTP sites, they would be 
outside the purview of the regular newsgroup creation guidelines.
He was very convincing in this respect as well.

So, if you have a mailing list that is currently eating up Internet
bandwith, you can create an inet distribution newsgroup with a 
two-way gateway, with the intent of decreasing the bandwidth used.
Of course, nowadays, nearly every site accepts messages with an
inet distribution, whether they are on an Internet connected network
or not.

If you want to create an inet group, contact fair@apple.com .
Make your subject line clear, and the body of the message brief,
and he will handle it quickly. If you ask for help, it will take 
ages and ages.

Rowan
